cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use apatools in your work, please cite it as below, and cite the engines that produced your results (see the software page of the documentation)."
type: software
title: "apatools: a toolbox for statistical analysis and APA-compliant reporting"
abstract: >-
  Wrappers around established Python and R tools (statsmodels, spreg, linearmodels, semopy, psmpy, lavaan,
  plm, splm) that return tidy tables with the statistics a manuscript needs, together with specification tests,
  effect conversions and reliability coefficients. The methods are benchmarked against independent references,
  and the documentation discloses design decisions, caveats and differences from R.
authors:
  - family-names: Valko
    given-names: Danila
version: 0.3.0
license: MIT
url: "https://ellariel.github.io/apatools/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ellariel/apatools"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/apatools/"
keywords:
  - APA reporting
  - meta-analysis
  - effect size
  - regression
  - spatial regression
  - panel data
  - structural equation modeling
  - propensity score matching
